codex
A second hard contradiction has emerged: `FragGrid`’s `G` is not “the window frame count”; it is the union of frames containing real fragment points. Replacing it with the full local axis changes Pearson centering and normalization unless a window-level used-frame mask is retained. Dense storage can remove the copied `(slot,intensity)` payload, but not automatically all grid semantics.
