docs/reviews/integer-tracing-2026-09-03/codex.md:13:| Termination mode | Default is `trace_termination_criterion="outlier"` with `trace_termination_outliers=5`; speXtract never overrides it. Because the test is `consecutive_missed > 5`, termination occurs after six consecutive misses. [`MassTraceDetection` ctor](/Users/kohlbach/Claude/OpenMS/src/openms/source/FEATUREFINDER/MassTraceDetection.cpp:26), [`run_()`](/Users/kohlbach/Claude/OpenMS/src/openms/source/FEATUREFINDER/MassTraceDetection.cpp:540) | **SET.** The sketch instead stops on sample rate. |
docs/reviews/integer-tracing-2026-09-03/codex.md:14:| Role of `min_sample_rate` | Under the active default, it does not terminate extension. It is a final validity test in `isTraceValid_()`. [`isTraceValid_()`](/Users/kohlbach/Claude/OpenMS/src/openms/source/FEATUREFINDER/MassTraceDetection.cpp:445) | **SET.** The design’s central account of the algorithm is wrong. |
docs/reviews/integer-tracing-2026-09-03/codex.md:15:| Sample-rate semantics when explicitly enabled | OpenMS waits until a direction has visited more than five scans, then computes one combined rate from both directions plus the apex. It is not a fresh per-direction `hits/visited`. | **SET.** Especially different near gaps and asymmetric peaks. |
docs/reviews/integer-tracing-2026-09-03/codex.md:16:| Final sample-rate denominator | OpenMS uses `trace.size() / (total_scans_visited - terminal_misses_down - terminal_misses_up)`. Internal misses remain; trailing misses are removed. | **SET.** The sketch has no equivalent final check. |
docs/reviews/integer-tracing-2026-09-03/codex.md:26:| When peaks become used | OpenMS collects provisional indices and marks them visited only after the entire trace passes length and sample-rate validity. [`run_()`](/Users/kohlbach/Claude/OpenMS/src/openms/source/FEATUREFINDER/MassTraceDetection.cpp:650) | **SET, severe.** The sketch/current code marks immediately and never rolls back an invalid trace, permanently deleting its peaks from later valid traces. |
docs/reviews/integer-tracing-2026-09-03/codex.md:33:| Valley splitting | The OpenMS path invokes `ElutionPeakDetection` inside `detectTraces_()`. [`detectTraces_()`](/Users/kohlbach/Claude/speXtract/src/DIAPseudoSpectra.cpp:1373) | **SET.** The integer branch currently bypasses it entirely at [the window dispatch](/Users/kohlbach/Claude/speXtract/src/DIAPseudoSpectra.cpp:2969). |
docs/reviews/integer-tracing-2026-09-03/codex.md:55:- Empty scans and scans whose peaks were filtered are absent. Ranking compresses those gaps.
docs/reviews/integer-tracing-2026-09-03/codex.md:130:| 1 | Wrong termination/tolerance semantics: outlier versus sample-rate, ±3σ and re-estimation versus fixed ppm, alternating directions versus sequential | Large changes in trace count and length distribution; gappy traces disappear or over-extend; merged chromatographic modes; different apexes and peptide sets. |
docs/reviews/integer-tracing-2026-09-03/codex.md:137:| 8 | Frames are not explicitly RT-sorted on the integer path | The OpenMS path calls `wmap.sortSpectra()`; the slab path trusts arrival order. Non-streaming or alternate-converter input can produce backward/jumping profiles and incorrect gap termination. |
docs/reviews/integer-tracing-2026-09-03/codex.md:144:Of the four risks listed in the design, mobility ranking and `min_sample_rate` are correctly recognized but substantially understated. Seed order is medium rather than top-tier. A shared-`used` race is avoidable and currently not the principal problem; independent band-local ownership and invalid-trace consumption are more immediate.
docs/reviews/integer-tracing-2026-09-03/codex.md:159:4. **Build a semantic oracle from OpenMS.** Synthetic cases must cover: six consecutive misses, internal versus trailing gaps, invalid-trace rollback, used nearest candidate with an unused second choice, equal intensities, equidistant peaks, empty spectra, asymmetric peaks, dynamic SD, running IM centroid, singleton MS2 traces and max-length rejection.
docs/reviews/integer-tracing-2026-09-03/codex.md:165:7. **Compare one representative window before parallelization.** Record peak-membership mapping, trace count, length, gap rate, apex/centroid coordinates, EPD split count and elapsed time. Peptide identity is a later gate, not the only correctness oracle.
docs/reviews/integer-memory-2026-09-03/codex.md:389:- targeted cases for equal intensities, flat valleys, two-point traces, and RT gaps.
docs/reviews/window-loop-perf-2026-09-03/vibe.md:134:### The dominant gap: **correlation kernel work volume**
docs/reviews/window-loop-perf-2026-09-03/vibe.md:150:**The 3.1× CPU gap is **almost entirely explained by the correlation kernel’s O(G) vs O(|support|) work**.
docs/reviews/window-loop-perf-2026-09-03/vibe.md:257:- **The algorithm does ~3× more work in the correlation kernel** (O(G) vs O(|support|)) and **no amount of tuning closes that gap entirely** — diaTracer’s design is fundamentally more efficient for sparse fragments.
docs/reviews/window-loop-perf-2026-09-03/vibe.md:261:- **`logoverlap` (Rank 5) is the nuclear option** — it would close **>50%** of the CPU gap to diaTracer, but **requires a full retune and peptide validation**.
docs/reviews/window-loop-perf-2026-09-03/vibe.md:263:**The 3.1× CPU gap to diaTracer is real and **primarily algorithmic**: the Pearson-over-grid design is the root cause. The mitigations above can recover **~30–40% of that gap**, but **not all of it** without switching correlation statistics entirely.
docs/reviews/integer-tracing-v2-2026-09-03/codex.md:7:| [L822](/Users/kohlbach/Claude/speXtract/src/DIAPseudoSpectra.cpp:822) | Emptiness is tested on the original slab. OpenMS first deletes every peak `<= noise`, then tests `spec.empty()`. A frame containing only below-noise peaks is therefore empty to OpenMS but non-empty here; this code calls `best()`, fails, and increments `missed`. Six such frames can terminate a direction, and trailing ones are incorrectly removed from the sample-rate denominator. | **SET** |
docs/reviews/integer-tracing-v2-2026-09-03/codex.md:90:The band cores cover the full TOF range without gaps, but semantic ownership is not shared.
docs/reviews/integer-tracing-v2-2026-09-03/codex.md:114:- `noise=10`, `snr=3`, `min_len=0`, `min_sample_rate=-1`, `max_len=-1`, `mass_ppm=15`, `im_tol=0.01`.
docs/reviews/integer-tracing-v2-2026-09-03/codex.md:124:The seven-gap assertion would have failed the first implementation because it lacked OpenMS’s `>5` consecutive-outlier termination and would bridge or reject the wrong span. The one-gap assertion catches premature termination.
